{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Acrylic latex by emulsion polymerisation: planned study",
  "notes": "Planned Box-Behnken study for a semi-batch emulsion copolymerisation of butyl acrylate and methyl methacrylate (about 50 % solids) in a 3 L reactor. Initiator and surfactant levels, monomer feed time and reaction temperature are varied; the runs are in randomised order and have not been carried out yet. Before each batch, record the MEHQ inhibitor content of the monomer charge (HPLC) and the cooling water supply temperature in the environmental columns. After the batch, measure the Z-average particle size by dynamic light scattering, the Brookfield viscosity at 25 °C, the coagulum retained on a 100 µm sieve, and residual monomer by headspace GC.",
